docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-28-| 2 | R3 and C* are equivalent within ±0.05, R3 lower, under two attack families | Report Q1 lines 9 to 18 | **Narrower.** The point estimates reproduce. "Equivalent" depends on the margin, and "two families" is mostly one (problems 1, 2). |
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-29-| 3 | Priority phase and newest-first targeting are substitutes | Report line 32 | **Supported** for the prescribed searches. The direct reading is stronger: the priority phase adds −0.001 once newest-first targeting is on. |
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-30-| 4 | B3 to R3 gain reduction replicates on 3 of 6 fresh markets | Report lines 23 to 29, `audit.json` | **Supported as stated.** |
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-31-| 5 | Welfare attacks and mixtures lower efficiency to 0.84 and 0.92 to 0.95 | Report lines 170 to 181, `posthoc.json` | **Narrower.** The 0.84 result is solid. The mixture result is arithmetic on two existing points, and the W1 search returned the null policy (problem 8). |
