docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-90-Quote (p. 6): "by the development tuning objective, which combines gross efficiency and attacker gain".
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-91-- The objective is min((eff − 0.90)/0.90, (0.30 − gain)/0.30) (design 4.1). The first term is at most 0.111. The second binds only if gain exceeds 0.267.
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-92-- C*'s score is 0.1032 (ledger 3.2). That is an efficiency of 0.993. Gain did not enter the choice (my reasoning).
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md:93:- **Effect.** Q1 compares on gain against a comparator chosen on efficiency. A gain-selected comparator can change the direction label.
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-94-- **Fix (analysis on existing records).** Report the gains of all 12 configurations. If another has lower gain, run it on the fresh markets (needs compute).
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-95-
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-96-**6 → Corollary 1 is correct but close to a restatement, and the abstract drops its conditions.**
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-97-Quote (abstract): "immediate free replacement makes the ban costless."
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-98-- The corollary assumes that replacement restores the same state distribution. The zero continuation loss then follows at once.
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-99-- The real content is the check for B2 and B3. That is one parenthesis and three proof lines.
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-100-- Hidden conditions: honest rivals that do not react, re-entry with no lost round, no identity memory in B2's price posting (not checkable).
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-101-- **Fix (text only).** State it as a remark with the conditions. Prove the B2 and B3 check from the rule definitions.
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-102-
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-103-**7 → Lemma 2 is correct but proves less than the text suggests.**
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-104-- It counts audits. It says nothing about deterrence. The term "audit dues" suggests a charge.
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-105-- The persistence remark is correct only while the identity is uniquely newest (see problem 4).
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-106-- "Served newest first" uses "served" for audits; elsewhere it means allocation.
docs/revision/roster/fable52-paper-r1.md-107-- The design measures age from the first offer (design 3.2). The paper says "younger than L rounds". An identity that offers but wins no jobs can age out unaudited.

